{"total_count":3,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482/events","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/482","id":1350156343,"node_id":"I_kwDOGiE5WM5QecA3","number":482,"title":"[Discussion] What middleware do you want?","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":45,"created_at":"2022-08-25T00:23:59Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T22:43:44Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"From v2.0.0, we can create 3rd party middleware. So far, the following 3rd-party middleware has been created.\r\n\r\n* GraphQL Middleware\r\n* Firebase Auth Middleware\r\n* Validator Middleware\r\n* Sentry Middleware\r\n\r\nGraphQL Middleware was originally provided as Built-in Middleware, which I also use. Firebase Auth make more authentication options for Cloudflare Workers. Validator Middleware is my creation, and I like it. Sentry Middleware will be very helpful in catching errors at the edge.\r\n\r\nNext, What middleware do you want?\r\n\r\nIf there is any Middleware you want, please comment here, even if you don't make it yourself. Someone may make it. You may also get other ideas by seeing the ideas here.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/482/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039/events","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/3039","id":2373359690,"node_id":"I_kwDOGiE5WM6NdphK","number":3039,"title":"Built-in validator formData parsing","user":{"login":"HugeLetters","id":119697239,"node_id":"U_kgDOByJvVw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119697239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters","html_url":"https://github.com/HugeLetters","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HugeLetters/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":5831663291,"node_id":"LA_kwDOGiE5WM8AAAABW5geuw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"D69931","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2024-06-25T18:24:21Z","updated_at":"2024-07-01T07:29:35Z","closed_at":"2024-07-01T07:29:35Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of Hono are you using?\n\n4.46\n\n### What runtime/platform is your app running on?\n\nNodejs\n\n### What steps can reproduce the bug?\n\nIs there a reason at this you use arrayBuffer to construct formData record?\r\nhttps://github.com/honojs/hono/blob/d21f8eb27aa43da9cd9d5b6f666692c4e92a0344/src/validator/validator.ts#L92\r\n\r\nHono has a built-in for that already `c.req.parseBody()`\r\n\r\nThis causes a bug if there's middleware which uses `.parseBody()` before validator - this populates `c.req.bodyCache.parsedBody` AND `c.req.bodyCache.formData`.\r\nAnd since your validator tries to check the cache for `formData`(not `parsedBody`) - it gets a hit which contains `FormData`, not a `Record`. \r\n\r\nIt seems this issue would be mitigated if either hono used `c.req.bodyCache.parsedBody` with a fallback to `arrayBuffer` or would just use `parseBody()` directly since it already checks the cache. \r\n\r\nSo is there some reason for the current behavior? Apologies that the issue isn't properly filled in but I hope my explanation is clear enough.\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\n_No response_\n\n### What do you see instead?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/3039/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393/events","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/1393","id":1874445413,"node_id":"PR_kwDOGiE5WM5ZLl7s","number":1393,"title":"fix(validator): cache `arrayBuffer` to use after validation","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2023-08-30T22:11:53Z","updated_at":"2023-09-03T05:43:03Z","closed_at":"2023-09-03T05:43:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/pulls/1393","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/1393","diff_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/1393.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/1393.patch","merged_at":"2023-09-03T05:43:02Z"},"body":"This PR enhances the handling of request bodies post-validation. After validating a JSON with the validator, you can now invoke `c.req.text()` to access the request body. Additionally, `c.req.text()` is now available `body` validation. We achieve this by caching the `arrayBuffer` in `c.req.bodyCache` and reusing it when calling `c.req.text()`.\r\n\r\nNote, if you attempt to use `c.req.raw.text()` after validating the `json` or `body`, you will encounter an error. Instead, always use `c.req.text()` in this context.\r\n\r\nFix #1387\r\n\r\n\r\n### Author should do the followings, if applicable\r\n\r\n- [x] Add tests\r\n- [x] Run tests\r\n- [x] `yarn denoify` to generate files for Deno\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/1393/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}